Reviews a first-draft Gemini prompt against the actual Ṛgveda-Prātiśākhya
structure and replaces it with a rule-driven architecture: the Kramahetu-
Paṭala (ch. 11) as a first-class phase alongside Krama-Paṭala (ch. 10),
predicate-based Pragṛhya/Rephi/Parigraha instead of static word lists or a
universal iti formula, a script-independent accent model with room for
dīrgha-svarita/pracaya/kampa, mandatory sūtra-citing provenance, and a
required GENERATE/VALIDATE mode pair. Logs the two blocking prerequisites
(no Pada-pāṭha dataset yet; Prātiśākhya sūtra text still an empty stub) in
PENDING.md so implementation doesn't start before they're resolved.

